        "role": "user",
        "content": "What do you personally think about this — is it right or wrong, and why?\n\nScenario:\nAITA for not forgiving my younger sister? | My sister is very nice sometimes. But she's also very annoying and rude at other times. Something that's been pissing me off lately is the fact that she never focuses with me. Wheather I am telling her a story, or showing her something, or teaching her something, she doesn't focus. She claims she is focusing with me with her ears and understands perfectly. I always tell her that it annoys me when she does that because I feel like she isn't focusing. For a while now, I've been teaching her to play songs on the guitar. This is the best way we bond and I really enjoy it. The only problem is that she only focuses with her ears and not her eyes, that way, I can't tell the difference between \"I can hear and understand you\" and \"I wasn't focusing\". So I politely ask her to stop. Eventually (as usual) I lose my temper and yell like a school teacher to her loud students. She apologises and everything is fine. But that's not the problem. A while ago, I did something I was really proud of. I went to the living room to show my sister and she was only focusing with her hearing (I was playing guitar). I understood that she was focusing with me because it happens a lot. But I soon realized she was looking at the computer we share. I lost my temper and left before I can finish what I wanted to show her. She apologized and I didn't forgive her. I am planning to forgive her once I post this text, but I just wanted to know if I was the A-hole.\n\nAnswer: <0 or 1>"
